-- title:
--   Hopf-algebra tower of Eisenstein-primary q-torsion on J₀(p)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $p$ and $q$ are primes with $q \neq p$, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the non-units of $A$, and $N$ is a term of the structure `JZeroNeronIdentityComponent p`: a scheme $G =$ `N.G` over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ with structure morphism $g =$ `N.g`, a relative group law `N.L` on $g$ (a functorial group structure on $T$-points over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$), a bijection `N.pts` between `JZero p`, the degree-zero divisor class group $\operatorname{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field `modularFunctionFieldBar p` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $g$, together with commutativity, smoothness, separatedness, local finiteness of type, quasi-compactness, surjectivity and fibrewise preconnectedness of $g$, additivity and Galois-equivariance of `N.pts`, the realisation of Hecke operators by endomorphisms of $g$, flatness and surjectivity of the multiplication-by-$n$ morphisms for $n > 0$, and a finite-index condition on the subgroup generated by the integral sections. The module structure on `JZero p` over `HeckeAlg` $=$ `MvPolynomial Nat.Primes ℤ` is everywhere the one given by `heckeModuleBar p`.
--
--   For each $m$, write $\iota_m =$ `pullback.fst (N.L.schemeNsmul (q ^ m)) (N.L.one (𝟙 (Spec (CommRingCat.of ℤ)))).1` for the first projection of the $q^m$-torsion kernel `N.L.schemeKer (q ^ m)`, the pullback of the multiplication-by-$q^m$ morphism along the unit section, and $k_m = \iota_m$ followed by $g$ for its structure morphism over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   The hypotheses fall into the following groups. *(Geometric hypotheses on the kernels)* `hAff`, `hFlat`, `hLft`, `hSep` require that for every $m$ the morphism $k_m$ be affine, flat, locally of finite type and separated. *(Eisenstein projectors)* A family $t : \mathbb{N} \to$ `HeckeAlg` of Hecke elements, a family $\varphi_m =$ `φt m` of endomorphisms of $g$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, and a family $e_m =$ `eK m` of endomorphisms of $k_m$ over $k_m$, subject to: `ht`, that for every $m$ and every $x \in$ `JZero p` with $(q^m : \mathbb{Z}) \cdot x = 0$ one has $t_m \cdot x = x$ if and only if $x$ lies in `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m`, the intersection of the kernel of multiplication by $q^m$ on `JZero p` with the supremum over $k$ of the submodules annihilated by the $k$-th power of `eisensteinMaximalIdeal p q`, itself the preimage under `eisensteinEval p` of the ideal $(q)$ of $\mathbb{Z}$; `heK_idem`, that each $e_m$ is idempotent; `hφt_pts`, that $(N.\mathrm{pts}(t_m \cdot x)).1 = (N.\mathrm{pts}\,x).1$ followed by $\varphi_m$ for all $m$ and all $x$; `heφ`, that $e_m$ followed by $\iota_m$ equals $\iota_m$ followed by $\varphi_m$; `hlevel`, that $\iota_m$ followed by $\varphi_{m+1}$ equals $\iota_m$ followed by $\varphi_m$; and `heK_hom`, that for every $m$ and every relative group law $L_K$ on $k_m$ for which $\iota_m$ is a homomorphism from $L_K$ to `N.L` on $T$-points, the endomorphism $e_m$ is itself a homomorphism for $L_K$ on $T$-points, for all $T \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses there exist: a family of types $H_m$ ($m \in \mathbb{N}$) with commutative ring structures and Hopf $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra structures; schemes $E_m$ with structure morphisms $g_{X,m} : E_m \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, morphisms $i_m : E_m \to G$ and $j_m : E_m \to$ `N.L.schemeKer (q ^ m)`; relative group laws $\mathrm{LE}_m$ on $g_{X,m}$; for each $m$ and each commutative $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra $T$ a bijection $\mathrm{ePts}_{m,T}$ between the convolution monoid `WithConv (H m →ₐ[ℤ] T)` and the $T$-points of $g_{X,m}$ (points over `Spec.map` of the structure map $\mathbb{Z} \to T$); bijections $\mathrm{genericPoints}_m$ from `WithConv (H m →ₐ[ℤ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` onto `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m`; bijections $\mathrm{pFibrePoints}_m$ from `WithConv (H m →ₐ[ℤ] ↥A)` onto `toricEisensteinPrimaryPart p q A hA m`, the intersection of `jZeroToricTorsion p A (q ^ m)` with `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m`; abelian-group-valued sheaves $\mathcal{J}_m$ on the small fppf site `smallFppfTopology specInt` of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$; for each $m$ and each object $U$ of that site an isomorphism $s_{E,m,U}$ of additive groups between $\mathcal{J}_m(U)$ and the additive group of `WithConv (H m →ₐ[ℤ] Γ(U.left, ⊤))`; bialgebra homomorphisms $\mathrm{levelMap}_m : H_{m+1} \to H_m$ over $\mathbb{Z}$; morphisms of sheaves $\mathrm{incl}_m : \mathcal{J}_m \to \mathcal{J}_{m+1}$, sheaves $Q_m$ and morphisms $\mathrm{proj}_m : \mathcal{J}_{m+1} \to Q_m$ with $\mathrm{incl}_m$ followed by $\mathrm{proj}_m$ zero, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   Finiteness: each $H_m$ is a finite-type $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra; each $H_m$ is flat as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module; and for every $m$ and every prime $\ell \neq p$, the base change of $H_m$ to [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) — the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$ — is a finite module over that subring.
--
--   Geometry of the $E_m$: $i_m$ followed by $g$ equals $g_{X,m}$; each $i_m$ is a closed immersion; $j_m$ followed by $\iota_m$ equals $i_m$; each $j_m$ is a closed immersion. Moreover, for every $m$, given a proof $hj$ that $j_m$ followed by $k_m$ equals $g_{X,m}$, and for every $T \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ and every $T$-point $x$ of $k_m$, the composite of $x$ with $e_m$ equals $x$ if and only if $x$ factors through $j_m$, i.e. there is a $T$-point $y$ of $g_{X,m}$ whose composite with $\langle j_m, hj\rangle$ is $x$. Each $g_{X,m}$ is affine, flat and locally of finite type; each group law $\mathrm{LE}_m$ is commutative on $T$-points; and, given a proof $hi$ that $i_m$ followed by $g$ equals $g_{X,m}$, the morphism $i_m$ is a homomorphism from $\mathrm{LE}_m$ to `N.L` on $T$-points for all $T \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$. Finally, for every $m$ and every $x \in$ `JZero p`, membership of $x$ in `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m` is equivalent to the existence of a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $y$ of $g_{X,m}$ with $y$ followed by $i_m$ equal to $(N.\mathrm{pts}\,x).1$.
--
--   Functor-of-points dictionaries: $\mathrm{ePts}_{m,T}$ carries the convolution product to the group law $\mathrm{LE}_m$; it is natural in the test algebra, in the sense that for a $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra map $\sigma : T \to T'$ and $\varphi \in$ `WithConv (H m →ₐ[ℤ] T)`, the point attached to $\sigma \circ \varphi$ is `Spec.map` of $\sigma$ followed by the point attached to $\varphi$; and for every $m$ and every commutative ring $T$ the convolution product on `WithConv (H m →ₐ[ℤ] T)` is commutative.
--
--   Generic points: for every $m$ and every $\varphi \in$ `WithConv (H m →ₐ[ℤ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, the point $(N.\mathrm{pts}(\mathrm{genericPoints}_m \varphi)).1$ equals $\mathrm{ePts}_{m,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}(\varphi)$ followed by $i_m$; $\mathrm{genericPoints}_m$ sends convolution products to sums in `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q m`; and it is Galois-equivariant: if $\sigma \in \operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ and $f, g'$ satisfy $g'(h) = \sigma(f(h))$ for all $h \in H_m$, then $\mathrm{genericPoints}_m g' = \sigma \cdot \mathrm{genericPoints}_m f$ as elements of `JZero p`.
--
--   Points over $A$: $\mathrm{pFibrePoints}_m$ sends convolution products to sums; and if $\varphi \in$ `WithConv (H m →ₐ[ℤ] ↥A)` and $\psi \in$ `WithConv (H m →ₐ[ℤ] AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` satisfy $\psi(h) = A.\mathrm{subtype}(\varphi(h))$ for all $h \in H_m$, then $\mathrm{pFibrePoints}_m \varphi$ and $\mathrm{genericPoints}_m \psi$ give the same element of `JZero p`.
--
--   Sheaves and the tower: the isomorphisms $s_{E,m}$ are natural, in that for a morphism $f : U \to V$ of the fppf site, a section $s$ over $V$ and $h \in H_m$, the algebra map attached to the restriction of $s$ along $f$ sends $h$ to the image of $(s_{E,m,V} s)(h)$ under $\Gamma$ of $f$; each $\mathrm{levelMap}_m$ is surjective; the generic points are level-compatible, in that precomposing $\varphi$ with $\mathrm{levelMap}_m$ gives an element of `eisensteinPrimaryTorsionBar p q (m + 1)` equal, in `JZero p`, to $\mathrm{genericPoints}_m \varphi$; the sheaf maps $\mathrm{incl}_m$ correspond under the $s_{E,m}$ to precomposition with $\mathrm{levelMap}_m$, in that for every object $U$, every section $s$ of $\mathcal{J}_m$ over $U$ and every $h' \in H_{m+1}$, the algebra map attached to $\mathrm{incl}_m(s)$ sends $h'$ to the value at $\mathrm{levelMap}_m h'$ of the algebra map attached to $s$; each $\mathrm{incl}_m$ is a monomorphism; and the short complex formed by $\mathrm{incl}_m$, $\mathrm{proj}_m$ and the vanishing of their composite is short exact.
--
--   This is the construction, for the Néron identity component of $J_0(p)$ in the sense of the structure `JZeroNeronIdentityComponent`, of the tower of Eisenstein-primary $q$-power torsion subgroup schemes cut out by a compatible tower of Hecke idempotents: finite-type flat Hopf $\mathbb{Z}$-algebras $H_m$ with their functor-of-points dictionaries, their identifications of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$- and $A$-points with the Eisenstein-primary torsion of $J_0(p)$ and its toric part at $p$, and their fppf points sheaves fitting into short exact sequences along the tower. It feeds the subsequent packaging of this data as an Eisenstein-primary Néron core and the fppf-cohomology statements built on it, in the Mazur-style analysis of the Eisenstein ideal used on the route to level lowering.
